 "reviewNotes": [
  "First year is the common engineering year; entering students take a math placement exam that may change the starting math course.",
  "Of the 21 core-elective hours: 3 creative arts, 3 social and behavioral sciences (DAEN: ECON 202 or 203, already in the plan), 3 language/philosophy/culture, 6 American history, 6 government.",
  "Grade of C or better required in the courses marked in the catalog's plan. (not checked)",
  "The 'Choose one: CHEM 120 or University Core Curriculum' slot in Year 1 Spring: CHEM 120 is for BMEN/CHEN/MSEN; Data Engineering students take a core course."
 ]
